{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "All new functions will be added to the configtx package in the standard Go module structure (github.com/hyperledger/fabric/common/configtx)",
    "Helper functions will return *config.Organization (or appropriate type) rather than a generic interface to maintain type safety and align with the existing configtx API",
    "Policy add/remove operations (U2, U3, U4) will follow the existing pattern used for similar operations elsewhere in configtx, using set/modify semantics rather than direct replacement",
    "U5 and U6 (add orderer/application org) will use a builder/fluent style that takes a config envelope and returns a new (mutated) envelope, allowing composition with other update functions",
    "U8 (cert revocation) will perform full X.509 chain validation: parsing the certificate, building the MSP's intermediate CAs root set, and confirming the cert chains to one of those CAs before adding to the revocation list",
    "Example tests will be added/updated under configtx/test (or equivalent) following the existing example test convention used in the repository",
    "Cryptographic operations in U8 will rely on standard library crypto/x509 plus the existing MSP crypto utilities rather than introducing new dependencies",
    "Functions that accept a config transaction will be designed so that the caller can chain further mutations; the function will not commit/sign the transaction"
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer has working knowledge of the existing Hyperledger Fabric configtx API and MSP config structure (FabricMSPConfig, revocation_list field, MSPConfig for various org types)",
    "The base proto-generated config structures (Application, Orderer, Consortium groups and their config groups) are available and do not require regeneration",
    "An existing helper for getting a config group from an envelope exists or can be reused (e.g., configtx.Get{Application,Orderer,Consortiums}FromConfigEnvelope); only thin wrappers are needed to obtain a specific org",
    "A consistent ID/name parameter convention is used across new functions (e.g., org name string), matching existing configtx conventions",
    "Certificate chain verification in U8 is performed in-memory using the MSP's configured CA/intermediate certs, without contacting a remote CA",
    "No new external dependencies are required; only standard library and existing fabric crypto utilities will be used",
    "Test certificates needed for U8 can be generated with existing test helpers in the fabric codebase (e.g., msp/test helpers) or via small inline test code",
    "Code review, CI integration, and merging are excluded from this estimate (only development work)",
    "Single developer working full time with no context-switching overhead to other projects"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and design",
      "activity_description": "Read the existing configtx package, identify where to add new helpers, draft function signatures, and decide common patterns (error handling, parameter ordering, return types) used across all eight user stories."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Get Organization Config (Application/Orderer/Consortium)",
      "activity_description": "Implement helper functions that, given a config envelope and an org name, return the config.Organization for the application, orderer, or consortium org groups. Add/update example tests demonstrating retrieval and reuse for a subsequent update."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Update Application org/group policies",
      "activity_description": "Implement functions to add and remove policies on the application org config group and the application group within the channel config. Update example tests to demonstrate adding a policy and chaining further updates."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Update Orderer org/group policies",
      "activity_description": "Implement functions to add and remove policies on the orderer org config group and the orderer group within the channel config. Update example tests to demonstrate the new behavior."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Update Consortium org/groups/consortiums policies",
      "activity_description": "Implement functions to add and remove policies on the consortium org config group, the consortium group, and the consortiums group. Update example tests covering all three levels."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Add Orderer Org to Channel",
      "activity_description": "Implement a fit-for-purpose function that takes the necessary orderer org parameters and produces a config envelope (or update) that adds a new orderer org to the channel configuration. Update example tests to demonstrate usage and chaining with subsequent updates."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Add Application Org to Channel",
      "activity_description": "Implement a fit-for-purpose function that takes the necessary application org parameters and produces a config envelope (or update) that adds a new application org to the channel configuration. Update example tests to demonstrate usage and chaining with subsequent updates."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Get MSP Config for an Org",
      "activity_description": "Implement a helper that retrieves the FabricMSPConfig for a given org (application, orderer, or consortium) from a config envelope so that callers can reuse CA certs or other MSP details. Update example tests to demonstrate usage."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Revoke Certificate from MSP",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function that, given a config block/transaction, an org name, and a certificate, verifies that the cert was issued by the org's MSP (using the MSP's root/intermediate CAs and X.509 chain validation), then mutates the FabricMSPConfig.revocation_list to include the cert. Return an error if the cert is not issued by the MSP. Add example tests covering both the success and negative (unrelated cert) cases."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Integration testing and bug fixing",
      "activity_description": "Run the full configtx test suite, fix any issues introduced by the new functions (signature mismatches, mutation vs. copy semantics, test interactions), and verify all new example tests pass end-to-end."
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Add GoDoc comments to all new public functions, ensure the example tests serve as runnable documentation, and update any package-level doc comments affected by the new API."
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 134
  }
}
```

